      "rationale": "Resolves a closed leaf from durable records, never from a worktree. It reads the leaf's recorded enclosure contract first. It then tries the recorded tree comparison: a leaf that recorded one reopens from its tree ids, and a leaf that recorded none proceeds to comparison-generation reopening with no converted/unconverted guard, then to the bare source range when no generation was published; an ambiguous or unreadable generation is refused rather than replaced. On a converted official line a leaf that recorded only a dataset comparison keeps its code sides and reports its knowledge sides legacy-unavailable, with no database read; legacy resolution uses the retained manifest's source sides.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
